    "chiefLastWords": "Understood — nothing publishes until you say so.\n\n**How I've made that structurally safe rather than just promising it**\n\nThe pages won't be built in `site/`. They'll be built in a new `preview/` folder that mirrors `site/`'s structure but is never copied to the server. You open it locally and it renders exactly as it will live, because it includes a copy of the stylesheet and the same relative paths. When you approve, the remaining step is mechanical: move two files into `site/` and add the footer link.\n\nThat footer link is worth naming plainly: **it is the switch.** A new page sitting in `site/` unlinked is already on the server after your next publish — technically live, just unreachable. So I'm holding both the files *and* the link.\n\n**The chain now on the board** — each step starts only when I accept the one before, which is my control point:\n\n- **T-1** Romanian text, every legal claim verified against primary sources — running now\n- **T-2** citation review: a reviewer opens every URL and confirms the cited article actually says what the page says\n- **T-3** English translation — law names kept in Romanian with an English gloss, British spelling to match your existing EN copy\n- **T-4** the two HTML pages, in `preview/`, following `evaluare.html`'s pattern\n\nOne judgment call I made without asking, since it matches the repo: \"buton\" becomes a plain `<a>` in the `footer > nav` row separated by `·`, not an HTML `<button>` — that's how your bottom menu already works.\n\n**Why I'",
